sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Student / Evaluator
    participant Browser as Web Browser (app.js)
    participant Server as Python HTTP Server (server.py)
    participant CBin as Native Binary (crowd_sim)

    User->>Browser: Selects particles (e.g. 10000), steps (100), threads (4)
    User->>Browser: Clicks "Run Simulation"
    Browser->>Browser: Validates client inputs & sets loading state
    Browser->>Server: POST /api/simulate (JSON payload)
    Server->>Server: Validates numeric ranges & acquires process lock
    Server->>CBin: subprocess.run([crowd_sim, --particles, ..., --json])
    Note over CBin: 1. Deterministic init<br/>2. Sequential run (timed)<br/>3. OpenMP parallel run (timed)<br/>4. Floating-point state compare<br/>5. Boundary audit<br/>6. Density grid computation
    CBin-->>Server: stdout (JSON string with metrics & grid)
    Server->>Server: Releases process lock
    Server-->>Browser: HTTP 200 OK (JSON response)
    Browser->>Browser: Populates Metrics Table (Time, Speedup, Efficiency)
    Browser->>Browser: Renders Density Heatmap on HTML Canvas
    Browser->>Browser: Updates Execution Log with verification status
    Browser-->>User: Displays completed dashboard & success badge
